It is my lunch break.
I am sitting in the canteen at my work.
I was busy yesterday.
Therefore I am calling the hairdresser now.
I take my mobile phone.
I call a hair salon in the city.
A woman answers the phone.
"Hello, this is the hair salon," says the woman.
"Hello, my name is Maya," I say.
"I would like to book an appointment on Thursday."
"One moment," says the hairdresser.
"Do you have an appointment in the afternoon?" I ask.
"Yes, we have an available appointment at half past four," she says.
"That suits me very well," I say.
"What is your phone number?" asks the hairdresser.
"My number is twelve, thirty-four, fifty-six, seventy-eight," I say.
"Thank you very much, see you on Thursday at half past four," she says.
"See you," I reply.
I put the phone on the table.
Now I finally eat my food.
